  "scope": "Complete strict Eucharistic Canon of the Rome 1635 Typographia Vaticana printing of the Missal recognized by Urban VIII, from the display title CANON MISSAE and red Sacerdos rubric on printed p. 245 through Per omnia saecula saeculorum, R. Amen and the red Iungit manus beside the chant staff on printed p. 249, before Oremus. Praeceptis salutaribus. Includes the display title, three red headings, all action rubrics and 25 printed crosses under a declared selective reading normalization that shares the letter-form conventions of roman-1570-canon-missae but keeps printed capitalization and punctuation. Excludes the prefaces and Sanctus before p. 245, the Crucifixion plate (Google page PA244), the Oremus, Pater noster and everything after it, and the retained title, Cum sanctissimum, Si quid est and colophon pages, which are identity and promulgation evidence only. Neither the whole Missal nor diplomatic glyph, accent or chant-pitch completeness is claimed.",
